Explicitly set the limit of open file descriptors (LimitNOFILE) for containerd after it has been removed since version 2.0, see https://github.com/containerd/containerd/blob/main/docs/containerd-2.0.md#limitnofile-configuration-has-been-removed

This change will not immediately affect existing nodes as containerd has to be restarted to take effect.
Restarting containerd is only save to do if the node has been drained in advance.
A node is drained automatically and rebooted during :doc:`Kubernetes upgrades </user/guide/kubernetes/upgrading-kubernetes>`
or when updating the host OS packages :ref:`update-kubernetes-nodes.sh<actions-references.update-kubernetes-nodessh>`.
If you require ``LimitNOFILE`` to be set immediately, please do one of these.
